WEBVTT

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.400
Once upon a time,

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.110
a boy posed a question to the great demon queen.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.990
“You always stare down at the world with such a sad face.”

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.660
“Are you going to do that forever?”

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.910
The queen answered:

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:29.040
“If you promise to grant my wish,

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.170
then I will stop being sad.”

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:42.020
“But if you break that promise, I will feast upon your flesh.”

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:48.770
A dream?

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.200
What’s the matter?

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.570
What do you mean “what’s the matter?”

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.780
Why are you in my bed aga—

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.330
What’s that?

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.080
Oh.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.960
Just something I keep because of a promise.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.210
A promise?

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.550
Yeah.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.380
Oh, Princess.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.590
Wasn’t someone just—

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:21.970
Geez…

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.470
In a proof by contradiction, if we assume there is a finite amount of prime numbers,

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:30.970
the left-hand side would be finite.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:36.180
The right-hand side, however, diverges into infinity, as it is a harmonic series.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.280
But this is a contradiction.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.540
By this method, we have disproved the possibility of a finite amount of prime numbers,

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.040
which had been our original assumption.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.620
Therefore, we are only left with the opposite,

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.330
and conclude that there must be an infinite amount of prime numbers.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.660
Quod erat demonstrandum.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.090
Proof complete.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:58.470
It’s perfect, Your Royal Highness.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.000
Call me Mina.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.080
In this room, I am but a student.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.110
I-I’m sor—

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.570
My apologies.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:18.390
No…

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.340
It’s almost like you’re some rare animal.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.030
Don’t you mean a fearsome beast?

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:38.330
You’re one to talk.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.180
I am the Queen of the Vampires.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:46.180
If I could not cause even one soul to fear me, my throne would be at risk.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:50.050
Even if I look like a lovely girl.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.720
Speak for yourself.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.680
The boys are playing soccer next!

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.550
Do not mind me.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:00.060
Go run around to your heart’s content.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.810
I will be fine on my own.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:02.810
But…

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.310
Oh? Are you worried for me?

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.870
No, for the others.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:07.790
Hush.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:10.910
I am, at present, a mere student.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:16.660
So long as I am, I will flawlessly accomplish all of my tasks.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.200
Now then,

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:23.120
you will all be cooking a beef and potato stew as well as an omelet.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.130
Although…

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:30.020
Your Royal Highness, will you be—

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.300
Call me Mina!

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.550
Do not mind me.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.230
Cooking one or two dishes is not a difficult task.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.640
Do you know what this tool is?

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:38.610
A razor.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.140
What about this one?

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:40.990
A tea whisk.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.810
Though it lacks in elegance.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.190
Well…

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.730
Who would be willing to pair up with Mina-san?

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.530
I’ll be her partner.

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:10.220
I apologize for the trouble.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.380
Not at all.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:15.350
I also wanted to talk… Your Royal Highness…

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:17.840
Like I said, you can just call me Mina.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.390
Well then, how should we begin?

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:24.600
Let’s see… Can you crack a few eggs?

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.810
Eggs… Eggs…

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.940
Very well!

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:35.570
Your Highness?

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.710
How could these eggs be so fragile and shatter from an impact like that?!

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.450
Are they not shells that shelter unborn life?

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.460
I see that you’ve never cooked.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.620
You jest!

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.010
There is nothing I cannot do!

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.880
It’s your first time, isn’t it?

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:55.430
Yes.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:57.840
That’s unfair.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:00.720
Well…

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:05.350
The key to cracking an egg is to hit it on a flat surface, rather than a corner.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.600
You are quite impressive.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.730
Did you know?

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.720
Omelets are Akir—

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.730
…Kaburagi-kun’s favorite.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:17.570
What?

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.620
Then, I must learn how to prepare them.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:22.250
But how do you know this?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:26.740
Th-That’s because he’s a classmate.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:27.660
I see.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.750
Let us begin, then.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:33.250
Now…

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:40.350
This was my first conversation with Princess Mina.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:42.940
She was arrogant and confident,

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:47.860
yet from time to time, showed weakness with unimaginable elegance.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.600
She was such a mysterious girl.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:54.270
But at the time, I wasn’t aware of anything.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.040
How terrifying she truly was…

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:00.540
…or how truly sad she was.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.000
Well, then.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.210
Bon appétit!

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:32.640
It’s great!

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:33.810
Truly?

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.310
Did you really make this?

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:37.280
But of course.

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:38.040
Go on.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:39.500
Feast upon the stew as well.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:40.960
I’m quite proud of it.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:43.030
Gladly then.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:45.570
I’m starving from running around so much.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:51.790
It is I.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.670
What? The TV?

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:59.040
According to our most recent report,

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.770
Prime Minister Mizoguchi will not approve the Special District Establishment Bill,

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.470
which was proposed by the anti-partisan union,

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:08.760
and will even go as far as calling for the dissolution of Parliament.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:14.480
In response, the representative of the union, Mr. Isurugi, replied to this statement with—

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.810
Very well. I am on my way.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:17.610
Yes.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:19.790
Summon Alphonse just in case.

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:21.280
Understood, Vera?

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:24.400
I will be leaving early.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.910
Something requiring my attention has come up.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.030
All right.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.030
I’ll get ready.

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:29.910
No.

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:31.620
I will be going alone.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:33.550
You are to stay in class.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.370
This is politics.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:37.260
I have no use for you there.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:38.540
But…

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.010
Are you going to watch?

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:48.440
It isn’t here.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:49.520
What isn’t?

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.720
Something Akira-kun asked for.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:55.060
Apparently, he lost a ring.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.060
A ring?

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.480
What does that mean?

00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:59.830
He couldn’t have wanted to give it to Her Highness, could he?

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:03.070
He’d better not be planning something like that.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:04.570
Nella.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:05.960
Yes?

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:08.070
Alphonse-sama has summoned you.

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:12.120
Is that so?

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.160
Yes.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:15.000
I’ve been keeping watch since this morning.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.120
Akira really is that vampire’s pet.

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.630
I’m truly disappointed.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:25.520
That would mean we must protect the students with everything in our power.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:28.270
We don’t want anyone to follow after President Shinonome.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:29.640
Wait!

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:30.760
That’s just a rumor.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.720
I understand how you feel, Kuze-kun.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:34.190
But…

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.810
Will you feel the same way after you see these?

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:44.150
They were delivered anonymously to the Student Council this morning.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:46.400
Now then…

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.710
I am short on time.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.030
Try to keep it brief.

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.500
Keep what brief?

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:55.120
You have some business with me, no?

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:57.290
Then can I ask you something?

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:57.840
What?

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:01.430
It’s about Shinonome Nanami, the Student Council President.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:06.260
The school is treating her as absent, but is that truly the case?

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:07.430
What are you implying?

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:09.970
This is only a rumor, but…

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:15.230
…maybe the President’s missing because she’s been bitten by a vampire.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:16.220
Oh?

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:18.350
Do you doubt me?

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:20.610
Are you suggesting I was behind this?

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:21.730
Yes.

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:26.440
You are quite the brave little girl.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:30.500
That ring…

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:32.460
Is something the matter with it?

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.580
I gave that to Akira-kun.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:36.670
Why?

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:39.960
I received this from Akira, as a sign of loyalty.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:40.580
You’re lying!

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:41.620
That can’t be!

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:42.590
How could it not?

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:43.880
Because…

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:47.680
Because I gave it to Akira-kun as a present last year.

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:50.180
<i>Just something I keep because of a promise.</i>

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:51.720
I see.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:52.680
You…

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.930
It was you.

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:02.570
Akira-kun would never give away something he received as a gift.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:03.570
Why do you—

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:04.940
Silence, little girl.

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:11.030
You seem to know quite a bit regarding Akira, so I will tell you something else about him:

00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:13.210
Akira is mine.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:17.160
Akira was born and raised to serve me, and me alone.

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:21.960
He is mine down to his last bit of bone, his last strand of muscle, and his last drop of blood.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:25.380
If you understand, then be gone from my sight.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:26.800
I am busy!

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:34.720
That Princess is as mysterious as ever.

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:35.680
Please, don’t!

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:36.610
Let’s talk this over!

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.610
Just shut up!

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:48.570
Kaburagi…

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.400
What the hell are you doing?

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:51.660
Damn, it’s an executive!

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:56.160
Are you all right?

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:57.410
What happened—

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:58.340
Don’t come any closer.

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:04.160
We’ll be jumped again if they see us talking to you!

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:06.040
You idiot! Don’t talk back to Kaburagi!

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:06.640
He’s right.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.790
We don’t want to be next!

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:10.460
You know what happened to the President!

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:11.380
What?

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:14.640
What do you mean, “like the President”?

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:16.300
Don’t tell me you don’t know.

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:18.900
Look.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.600
The President?

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.100
She’s been absent for a long time.

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:28.860
At least, that’s what we thought.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:30.700
But this is the truth.

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:34.070
Look closely. This was in the Student Council Room.

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:38.710
It’s completely totaled, but the room was perfectly fine by sunrise.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.290
Who’s the only person that could do that?

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:43.670
The person who rules above all vampires.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:49.050
Do you still plan to side with the vampires, Kaburagi Akira?

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:56.300
Is something on your mind?

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:57.010
No.

00:11:57.930 --> 00:12:01.520
Do you believe Mizoguchi will truly call for the dissolution of Parliament?

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:02.510
Most likely.

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:09.700
The current situation suggests that the bill will be passed by the senators we spoke to.

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:12.780
And if that were to happen?

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:17.080
It would be quite difficult to acquire as many seats as we currently have.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.540
And?

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:19.790
Please take a look.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:22.280
He is the Prime Minister’s five-year-old grandson.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:27.080
Despite his public appearance, he’s a gentle grandfather who adores his grandson.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:28.210
Alphonse.

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:31.840
You may have to work much earlier than I had thought.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.130
As you wish.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:34.930
If that is your will.

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:38.720
Someone is backing the Academy and Mizoguchi.

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:41.390
This is the turning point of our battle.

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:54.530
Isn’t it humiliating to be treated like an idiot?

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:59.370
I’ll save you.

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:04.870
It’s like a dream. That city…

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:06.500
But, it’s an inescapable reality.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:09.880
To me, and to all humans.

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:11.790
Why are you saying it like that?

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:14.800
It’s as if you’re saying that you’re not one of us.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:19.930
Did you like the food?

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:21.390
Yeah.

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:24.220
It tasted much better than it looked.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.560
That’s good to hear.

00:13:25.560 --> 00:13:28.280
The Princess was really trying her best.

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:30.400
Thanks, Yuki.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:33.410
You added the flavor, right?

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:36.570
It tasted like your food.

00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:39.540
And vampires, unlike humans, don’t have taste buds.

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:42.580
They couldn’t possibly cook.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:48.250
But considering the Princess’ personality,

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:50.590
she’d never say she can’t do something.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.380
I was worried that she didn’t even thank you.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:57.590
I guess you really understand her.

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:58.760
The Princess.

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:01.850
That’s…

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:14.320
These guys…

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.160
Vampires!

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:30.590
They’re wearing our uniform!

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:38.340
So you will reject us no matter what?

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.760
Of course.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:43.840
Perhaps it is impossible for us to come to an agreement.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:47.080
In this day and age, could Japan really accept this,

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:49.180
especially when it involves vampires?

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:52.270
How could you expect us to agree to these concessions?

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:56.650
Wasn’t the reward I had prepared more than sufficient?

00:14:56.650 --> 00:15:00.530
Despite that, or rather, <i>because</i> of that fact,

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:02.510
we should see if the people wish for that,

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:04.730
to see if they truly view that as a blessing,

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:07.540
and ask the citizens if they want the dissolution or not.

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:09.830
Ask the citizens?

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:11.450
It sounds beautiful,

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:14.870
but it’s merely a statesman avoiding a grave decision.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:15.870
Oh?

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:18.140
If we were to pull out of here right now,

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:22.510
Japan would plummet into an unfathomable depression.

00:15:22.510 --> 00:15:25.220
Recovery would be nearly impossible.

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.550
What about it?

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:31.520
If the citizens chose it themselves, they’d surely accept it.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:37.230
Now that I recall, you just have one more year left in office.

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:38.200
Yes.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.280
So you don’t care about what’s to come.

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:43.440
I see.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.290
By fearlessly resisting against us vampires, us monsters,

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:50.000
it creates the image of you protecting the dignity of Japan…

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:53.920
…and will glorify your name for many years to come.

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:56.620
You’re quite sharp for a little girl.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:01.260
If, and only if that happens,

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:04.930
then as a result, it’s true that my Mizoguchi family

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:10.390
may become a crucial existence to this country’s political system for generations to come.

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:14.980
You disgust me.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:16.900
Pardon?

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:21.400
Prime Minister, we are monsters, just as you’ve said.

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:24.820
We can subdue anyone with fear and power.

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:29.540
But why do you think we chose to speak with you instead?

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:32.490
That is because

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:36.250
we had decided to follow the rules of human society.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:39.540
We proposed a compromise to you out of respect.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:42.400
If you continue to talk down to us,

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:46.350
we will merely do things our way.

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:50.600
A-Are you threatening this country?!

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:53.100
I am still talking with you right now.

00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:55.390
What does that mean?

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:58.480
Where is your respect for the Prime Minister?!

00:16:58.480 --> 00:16:59.940
Who are you to speak of respect?

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:02.900
Get off your high horse, little girl!

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:04.360
I suppose this is it, then.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:08.370
Do it.

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:09.830
As you wish.

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:11.660
Nella.

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:23.130
This conversation is over.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:26.720
I am very sorry things had to end this way,

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:28.720
Prime Minister Mizoguchi.

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:50.950
Akira-kun!

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:02.870
It really worked!

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:05.930
Did you like the silver dust, doggy?

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.930
You’re an eyesore.

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.810
Stay the hell away from Her Royal Highness!

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:17.480
Die!

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:37.000
You’re…

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:42.710
Leave this to me.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:48.300
Akira-kun!

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:50.210
Just get out of here.

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:51.180
You’re in the way.

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:05.440
Those guys were wearing our uniform.

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:06.860
Damn it.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:10.320
There are vampires in our school?

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:12.700
I need to hurry and tell the Princess.

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:17.450
You’re still thinking about her over yourself in this situation?

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:26.830
Do you remember when I suddenly collapsed on the school grounds?

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:33.890
Well, on that day I collapsed, the Princess came to see me all by herself.

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:38.180
All for some stupid promise when I was little.

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:41.140
She didn’t care that her life was in danger.

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:43.930
So I…

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:45.400
She wasn’t alone.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:50.030
I saw you two.

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:53.410
On that day, when you and Mina-san were running away…

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:57.410
…and all of those escorts were following close behind,

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:59.960
protecting you.

00:20:02.370 --> 00:20:03.080
Are you serious?

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:25.140
Your Highness?

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:28.870
I’m sorry. Could you leave me alone for a while longer?

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:46.420
Akira-ku—

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:55.880
Akira?

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.180
What are you doing right now?

00:20:57.510 --> 00:20:58.470
Well…

00:20:58.470 --> 00:20:59.970
What about you?

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:02.050
Nothing very important.

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:06.190
I just wanted to hear your voice.

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:08.100
Hey, Princess.

00:21:08.690 --> 00:21:10.690
I can really…

00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:12.650
…trust you, right?

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:25.330
Yes.

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:35.170
Trust me.

00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:38.280
Dance with the Vampire Maids.

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:38.970
Part Five!

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.970
Her Highness gave me the beef and potato stew she cooked!

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:44.240
Let’s play rock-paper-scissors for it.

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:45.040
What about Nella?

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:46.600
It’s her loss for not being here.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:47.980
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:48.940
I win!

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:50.410
You were late!

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.470
But I’m usually slow.

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:52.480
What are you up to?

00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:54.190
It’s Her Highness’ beef and potato stew.

00:21:54.190 --> 00:21:54.750
Shh!

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:56.110
What were <i>you</i> up to?

00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:57.490
Kidnapping some kid.

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:00.650
It’s from Her Highness.

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:01.740
I’m so happy.

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:02.960
How is it?

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:04.150
There’s no taste.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:06.000
Well, you’re a vampire.
